English Translation:
## 3. ENGLISH TRANSLATION

**[Continuation from previous folio...]**

...as is befitting to promise to the prince. Confiding in you on account of your proven faith, industry, and probity—not revoking but rather confirming any previous commission and power granted by us to you or to others as follows in our name to be committed and mandated—which [matters] were executed by us and [to the end] that perfectly on behalf of the said lord King beyond the mountains [*ultramonium*] and on behalf of all his [matters], you [shall take] from the goods, and corporeal and real possession of whatsoever parcels, and apprehending [them] in my name and on our behalf, [making] a public inventory by means of and expressly with movable goods which for the treasury [*thesauraria*] we wish to be received by you and held;

And from all the castles, vills, and places aforesaid, and from all others whatsoever, receiving homage and [oaths] of fidelity and the praiseworthy and customary oath in my name and on our behalf, [for] each of those places, which [pertain to] the aforesaid vills, castles, and places themselves, and to others for whom [it is required] or shall be owed, and by right in our name: confirming all their privileges, liberties, franchises, immunities, fueros, usages, and customs by which and through which better or until now they have exercised [their rights over] the same castles, vills, places, and goods, and the boundaries and vassals dwelling in those castles, vills, and places—ruling, governing, defending, and administering on our behalf;

And in those [places] for which, according to God and judgment, [there is] *merum et mixtum imperium* [high and low justice] and any other jurisdiction whatsoever, they may use and may be able to [exercise] that *merum et imperium*: to punish and by any sentence whatsoever fully and [to] deprive, to command penalty and remission [of penalties], to provide officials in the said castles, vills, and places; and [with power to] exhibit and appoint the same or others as they may [see fit]; who on our behalf in my name [and] on our behalf [may erect] gallows and half-gallows, pillories, and any other signs [signifying] jurisdiction, *merum et [mixtum] imperium*, and jurisdiction aforesaid to be erected and established;

And [to do] all things and through any official whatsoever to cause to be done and to hold justly. And [to perform] all other things both general and particular [...] to be done and to do and freely to exercise which in the premises and concerning them [are necessary], and with proper [authorities] over [such] offices;

Since concerning them and those [matters], we commit [to] you [the power] in constituting and making [arrangements] verbally thereupon, and [for] receiving on behalf of the said [matters] from movable goods, yours [and] ours, free and general administration, and we commit full [power], and also a certain account and form [...] to be rendered [for] things acted and done by you in the aforesaid [matters].

**Given at Barcelona** under our authentic seal, the 16th day of [month] in the year of the Nativity of the Lord one thousand three hundred ninety-three.

[Registration notation] V[?] de Ponte [?]

**[Subscriptio:]**
[Ordered/verified] by Franciscus de Aranda, [in the capacity of?] procurator general, for the treasurer [?], by his own [authority].

